From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Takashi Nakayama <tnak@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:11:43 -0700
Subject: ServiceWorker: Respect encoding for top-level worker scripts

Plumb the resolved TextEncoding of top-level classic worker scripts from
WorkerClassicScriptLoader and InstalledScriptsManager::ScriptData
through to ServiceWorkerScriptCachedMetadataHandler::Encoding().

This ensures that the script encoding is taken into account when
generating and matching V8 code cache for service worker scripts.
Guarded by the new runtime-enabled feature.

See the bug for details.

Bug: 552757015
Change-Id: Ie90932a1cd34f2251dd5346f1af3a32c095e3abc
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8523966
Commit-Queue: Shunya Shishido <sisidovski@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Shunya Shishido <sisidovski@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716269}

